.TH CHECKSMIX 1 "2026-09-22" "checksmix 0.3.14"
.SH NAME
checksmix \- run MMIX assembly or object files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B checksmix
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE...
.br
.B checksmix run
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE...
.br
.B checksmix check
.I FILE.mms...
.br
.B checksmix build
.RI [ \-o
.IR OUT.mmo ]
.I FILE.mms...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B checksmix
is an MMIX emulator. It can parse and execute MMIX assembly
.RB ( .mms )
directly, or load MMIX object files
.RB ( .mmo ).
.PP
When invoked with a file (or without a subcommand), the default behavior is
.BR run .
Multiple
.BR .mms
files are assembled into one shared symbol space before execution.
.PP
.B Subcommands:
.TP
.B run FILE...
Execute one or more program files. With a single
.BR .mms " or " .mmo
file, dispatches by extension. With multiple files (must all be
.BR .mms ),
assembles them into one shared symbol space, then executes.
.TP
.B check FILE.mms...
Parse and encode one or more
.B .mms
source files; prints any assembler warning to standard error and still
exits 0, with error messages and exit 1 on failure.
.TP
.B build [--output OUT.mmo] FILE.mms...
Assemble one or more
.B .mms
source files into a single
.B .mmo
object file. Multiple inputs are assembled into one shared symbol space.
.PP
.B build
and
.B run
print any assembler warning to standard error the same way
.B check
does; a warning never fails the run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-unsigned
Display register values as unsigned decimals in
.B run
mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-steps " " N
Stop
.B run
after
.I N
instructions if the program has not halted, the halting instruction counted
among the
.IR N .
Prints
\fBprogram did not halt within \fIN\fB instructions; @\~=\~#\fIHEX\fR
on stderr, naming
.I N
and
.BR @ ,
the address of the next instruction, and exits 124.
.I N
is a positive integer; without
.B \-\-max\-steps
a program runs until it halts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B run
exits with
.B $255
mod 256 when the program executes
.BR "TRAP 0,Halt,0" ,
and with 1 when assembly or loading fails or the machine halts any other
way. With
.BR \-\-max\-steps ,
.B run
exits 124 when the budget runs out; since a program halting with
.B $255
mod 256 = 124 exits 124 too, the stderr line tells the two apart.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Enable tracing output from the emulator. Example:
.BR RUST_LOG=checksmix=debug .
.SH FILES
These live in the source repository, not in the published crate, which
excludes
.IR examples/ .
.TP
.I examples/hello_world.mms
Minimal program using
.B TRAP 0,Fputs,StdOut
to print a string.
.TP
.I examples/linked_list.mms
Traverses a static linked list and sums node values.
.TP
.I examples/all_instructions_test.mms
Broad instruction coverage for regression testing.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run MMIX assembly directly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
checksmix examples/hello_world.mms
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check syntax of assembly source files without executing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
checksmix check examples/hello_world.mms
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build an object file from assembly source, writing
.I examples/hello_world.mmo
beside the source:
.PP
.RS
.nf
checksmix build examples/hello_world.mms
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run that prebuilt object file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
checksmix examples/hello_world.mmo
.fi
.RE
.PP
Assemble multiple source files into one shared symbol space, then run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
checksmix main.mms lib.mms
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or assemble them first, then run the object file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
checksmix build main.mms lib.mms -o /tmp/combined.mmo
checksmix /tmp/combined.mmo
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmixasm (1),
.BR mmixdb (1)
